2 0 obj
<<
/Producer (PyPDF2)
/Title (Consumption\040and\040Portfolio\040Choice\040over\040the\040Life\040Cycle)
/Author (Joao\040F\056\040Cocco\054\040Francisco\040Gomes\054\040Pascal\040J\056\040Maenhout)
/Subject (This\040article\040solves\040a\040realistically\040calibrated\040life\040cycle\040model\040of\040consumption\040and\040portfolio\040choice\040with\040non\055tradable\040labor\040income\040and\040borrowing\040constraints\056\040Since\040labor\040income\040substitutes\040for\040riskless\040asset\040holdings\054\040the\040optimal\040share\040invested\040in\040equities\040is\040roughly\040decreasing\040over\040life\056\040We\040compute\040a\040measure\040of\040the\040importance\040of\040human\040capital\040for\040investment\040behavior\056\040We\040find\040that\040ignoring\040labor\040income\040generates\040large\040utility\040costs\054\040while\040the\040cost\040of\040ignoring\040only\040its\040risk\040is\040an\040order\040of\040magnitude\040smaller\054\040except\040when\040we\040allow\040for\040a\040disastrous\040labor\040income\040shock\056\040Moreover\054\040we\040study\040the\040implications\040of\040introducing\040endogenous\040borrowing\040constraints\040in\040this\040incomplete\055markets\040setting\056\040Copyright\0402005\054\040Oxford\040University\040Press\056)
/Keywords (20\040Jun\0402005\054\040Review\040of\040Financial\040Studies\054\040Natural\040borrowing\040limit\054\040Consumption\040\050economics\051\054\040Portfolio\054\040Human\040capital\054\040London\040Business\040School\054\040INSEAD)
>>
endobj
